From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] credui: the credentials prompt without a target, authentication buffers, command line prompt, SSO

- CredPackAuthenticationBufferW and CredUnPackAuthenticationBufferW
  returned ERROR_CALL_NOT_IMPLEMENTED from BOOL functions (so "succeeded"
  having done nothing). A packed buffer is a KERB_INTERACTIVE_LOGON whose
  strings follow it, their buffers offsets from its start, as LsaLogonUser
  takes it; CRED_PACK_WOW_BUFFER gives the 32-bit layout,
  CRED_PACK_PROTECTED_CREDENTIALS protects the password with CredProtect
  (and unpacking with it unprotects it). The size needed comes back with
  ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_BUFFER; something that is not such a buffer is
  ERROR_NOT_CAPABLE; with no domain asked for, it is put in the user name.
  The A forms were missing.
- CredUIPromptForWindowsCredentials (W, and the missing A) was
  ERROR_CALL_NOT_IMPLEMENTED: the credentials dialog without a target
  ("Enter your credentials"), the user name from the input buffer or the
  current user (CREDUIWIN_ENUMERATE_CURRENT_USER), the check box with
  CREDUIWIN_CHECKBOX, what is entered packed into a CoTaskMemAlloc'd buffer
  (32-bit with CREDUIWIN_PACK_32_WOW); ERROR_CANCELLED on Cancel.
- CredUICmdLinePromptForCredentials (A and W, "@ stub"s): asks for the user
  name, the password (without echo on a console) and whether to save, on
  the console or from standard input; saves or keeps them for
  CredUIConfirmCredentials as the dialog does.
- CredUIPromptForCredentialsA, CredUIConfirmCredentialsA and
  CredUIParseUserNameA ("@ stub"s).
- CredUIStoreSSOCred and CredUIReadSSOCred were FIXMEs keeping nothing and
  finding nothing: a realm's (the default one's with none) user name and
  password are kept as a credential and the user name read back.
- CredUIInitControls initializes the controls the prompt uses;
  SspiPromptForCredentialsW's FIXME is a TRACE.

Gate: test/creduiwin-gate.sh (on Xvfb, test/creduiwin-probe.c). Mutants
SG_MUTANT_NO_UNPROTECT, SG_MUTANT_NO_SSO (credui/credui_main.c). Wine's
credui test: no failures.
